# Docker Registry Mirror Configuration
#
# Configure registry mirrors to avoid Docker Hub rate limiting and speed up image pulls.
# Mirrors should be HTTP/HTTPS proxy caches (e.g., Harbor, distribution/registry).
#
# The kind cluster will be configured to try the mirror first, then fall back to
# the upstream registry if the mirror is unavailable.

# Docker Hub mirror (registry-1.docker.io)
# Example: DOCKER_MIRROR=harbor.services.home.internal.randomvariable.co.uk/docker
#DOCKER_MIRROR=

# GitHub Container Registry mirror (ghcr.io)
# Example: GHCR_MIRROR=harbor.services.home.internal.randomvariable.co.uk/github
#GHCR_MIRROR=
